<section class="page-hero section-shell"><p class="eyebrow">Interactive coding lab</p><h1>Try Java while it’s still fresh.</h1><p>The Java Lab opens as a focused workspace with editor, diagnostics, source inspection, Scanner input, examples, and local project storage.</p><a class="button button-large" href="index.html">Open Java Lab →</a></section><section class="section-shell lab-limits"><h2>Honest learning environment</h2><div><article><strong>Supported subset</strong><p>This is not a full JDK. The lab tells you when a Java feature is outside its documented subset.</p></article><article><strong>Isolated execution</strong><p>Compiled programs run in a sandboxed iframe with a narrow message interface—never on the PHP server.</p></article><article><strong>Resource limits</strong><p>Execution time, source, input, output, and arrays are bounded to keep the workspace responsive.</p></article></div></section>
